From 1255b018c0ee4bc2288420b66071bf7b23f48a62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:50:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: controller: Offer the DC itself when an unknown node
 joins

When do_dc_join_offer_one() makes offers because of a join request, it
also makes one to the local node, to ensure the correct value for
max_generation_from. When it makes offers because an unknown node
joined, it does not. max_generation_from then keeps the value it had
when the join round began, and a rejoining node whose CIB is newer than
that becomes the source for the finalization sync.

do_dc_join_finalize() clears R_HAVE_CIB, sets it again only if
max_generation_from is the local node, and waits for any transition in
progress. If that transition fences the rejoining node, as when the node
rejoined while being fenced, there is nothing left to sync from.
R_HAVE_CIB is never set, and the DC stays in S_FINALIZE_JOIN, running
nothing, until join-finalization-timeout (30 minutes by default).

This became reachable with 0d91d682 (#3056), which made finalization
wait for a transition in progress. Before that, the DC finalized at
once, while the rejoining node was still there to sync from.

Now make an offer to the local node in this path too, as the join
request path does.

We observed this on a two-node cluster after corosync on one node died
and systemd restarted it while the DC was fencing that node.

Signed-off-by: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
---
 daemons/controld/controld_join_dc.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemons/controld/controld_join_dc.c b/daemons/controld/controld_join_dc.c
index 7c941c001..5f7ad8a56 100644
--- a/daemons/controld/controld_join_dc.c
+++ b/daemons/controld/controld_join_dc.c
@@ -345,6 +345,22 @@ do_dc_join_offer_one(long long action, enum crmd_fsa_cause cause,
         pcmk__info("Making join-%d offers to any unconfirmed nodes because an "
                    "unknown node joined", current_join_id);
         g_hash_table_foreach(pcmk__peer_cache, join_make_offer, &member);
+
+        /* As for a join request below: if an offer went out, make one to the
+         * local node as well.  Otherwise max_generation_from keeps whatever it
+         * was when this join round began, and a node whose CIB is newer than
+         * that becomes the source for the finalization sync.  If that node is
+         * then lost (fenced, say) before finalization, nothing is left to sync
+         * from, R_HAVE_CIB is never set, and the DC waits in S_FINALIZE_JOIN
+         * until join-finalization-timeout.
+         */
+        if (crmd_join_phase_count(controld_join_welcomed) > 0) {
+            member = controld_get_local_node_status();
+            if (controld_get_join_phase(member) != controld_join_welcomed) {
+                join_make_offer(NULL, member, NULL);
+            }
+        }
+
         check_join_state(cur_state, __func__);
         return;
     }
